.TH chown 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
chown \- change file owner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chown
.I "owner file ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chown
sets the owner of each
.I file
to
.IR owner ,
which is either a numeric uid or a name from
.BR /etc/passwd .
The group is left alone.
.SH OPTIONS
None.  There is no
.BR \-R ,
and the
.I owner:group
form is not accepted \- use
.BR chgrp (1)
for the group.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B chown
stops at the first file it cannot change and exits 1.  Files after that
one are not touched.
.SH NOTES
Only the superuser may give a file away.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chgrp (1),
.BR chmod (1)
